\section{Outer-loop optimization parameters}{

\code{PLNmixture_param()} adds parameters controlling the EM loop of the mixture and the smoothing; the other
entries of \code{config_optim} (\code{ftol_em}, \code{maxit_em}, \code{ftol_in}, ...) control the fits of the PLN components,
with the defaults of \code{\link[=PLN_param]{PLN_param()}}:
\itemize{
\item "ftol_out" EM loop of the mixture stops when the objective changes by less than ftol_out (relative). Default is 1e-3
\item "maxit_out" EM loop of the mixture stops when the number of iterations exceeds maxit_out. Default is 50
\item "it_smooth" number of the iterations of the smoothing procedure. Default is 1.
}

Until version 1.3.2, the EM loop of the mixture was controlled by \code{ftol_em} and \code{maxit_em}, which the PLN
components then shared (loose tolerances that stopped the EM loops of the components early).
}

